# Katon — environment variables.
# Copy to .env.local and fill in. NEVER commit real secrets.
#
# RULE (locked decision #5): secret/service keys are SERVER-ONLY. Never prefix a
# secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that exposes it in the client bundle.

# --- Supabase (server-only) ---
# Service role key bypasses RLS; it must stay server-side.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- Xendit (Phase 4a) ---
XENDIT_SECRET_KEY=
# The callback verification token from the Xendit dashboard. The webhook handler
# rejects any request whose x-callback-token header does not match this.
XENDIT_WEBHOOK_TOKEN=

# --- App ---
# Used to build the share link katon.app/r/<token>.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://katon.app

# MIRROR_PREVIEW_TOKEN is GONE (2026-08-23), and this note replaces it for the same
# reason the NEXT_PUBLIC_FREE_FULL_READING note below exists: a deleted variable
# left in a deploy is a variable someone will assume still does something.
#
# It was QA access to /api/mirror while that route was linked from nowhere - unset
# meant the route 404'd entirely, sent as an `x-mirror-preview-token` header rather
# than a query parameter. PROMOTION removed the requirement, which is exactly what
# this variable's own note said would happen, and lib/mirror/fence.js went with it.
# The funnel front door creates and reads mirror readings now.
#
# UNSET IT IN VERCEL. It is inert - no code reads it - but leaving a stale secret in
# a project's environment is how NEXT_PUBLIC_FREE_FULL_READING became architecture.
# Nothing replaces it: the mirror is the product, its ceiling is the rate limiter,
# and the paywall is `row.paid === true` in lib/deliver/handlers.js.

# NEXT_PUBLIC_FREE_FULL_READING is GONE (2026-08-05). It ungated the full reading
# for cafe tests, was left set in Vercel, and became the de facto architecture: the
# paywall never rendered in production and Xendit rejected the site for having no
# checkout. Deleted with lib/flags.js. Do not reintroduce it as an env var.

# ── THE RENDERER HAS ONE PROVIDER (CLAUDE.md rule 15) ──────
# Gemini, with module assembly as the failover. Ruled by Reyner 2026-08-22; the OpenAI
# secondary was deleted in the same commit. It had never run: arming it needed a model
# id no document in this repo ever named, so `openaiConfigured` returned false for the
# project's whole life and the chain skipped it every time.
#
# THE CONSEQUENCE IS OPERATIONAL, NOT ARCHITECTURAL. With no second provider, a Gemini
# outage or an exhausted balance is a 100% floor rate - every reader gets module
# assembly. The mitigation is a balance alert on the Gemini account, which does not
# exist yet and is in the deferred register.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
